# browser: its work is a file chosen in its navigator, whose title and list name the run folder, which differs between the oracle cut and a graded run.
# So the navigator is opened (Alt-f, after the opening still picture, the window mapped), taken up to the root by ../ (more clicks than any run folder is
# deep; at / a ../ stays at /), then into /cdrom, a folder of the machine that is empty on every road; no picture is taken between, so each line is the same
# on every road. Then the program quits by its own key, Alt-q.
move 100 100
keydown Alt_L
key f
keyup Alt_L
click 1 50 72
click 1 50 72
click 1 50 72
click 1 50 72
click 1 50 72
click 1 50 72
click 1 50 72
click 1 50 72
click 1 50 72
click 1 50 72
